{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB14568 - MONDO_18434",
  "verbalization": "Ivosidenib is associated with Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a pathway involving Idarubicin, which is indicated for AML. The evidence suggests that Ivosidenib may be repurposed for AML, as it shares indications with other AML subtypes, including those with the T(9;11)(p22;q23) translocation. This relationship is supported by the presence of overlapping indications between Ivosidenib and Idarubicin, which in turn are linked to AML with the specific chromosomal translocation. The shared indication for Idarubicin across different AML subtypes implies a potential mechanism of action that could be relevant to AML with the T(9;11)(p22;q23) translocation. The evidence suggests that Ivosidenib may be considered for use in this specific AML subtype due to its overlapping indications with Idarubicin, which is a known agent for this condition.",
